-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Expand the sentence bank.
--
-- The product spec says "each planet may contain approximately 50 key
-- sentences, selected based on the theme and frequency of everyday use" —
-- the sentence bank is the curriculum the live tutor teaches from, the
-- continuous audio it plays in the car, and the denominator of the
-- "sentences" progress metric. Until now the planets carried only a handful
-- each (Planet 1: 10, Planet 2: 5, Planet 3: 3, Planets 4-8: 6), which left
-- the tutor and the audio with almost no material.
--
-- This migration authors a substantial new set per planet (Planet 1 -> 40
-- total, Planet 2 -> 30, Planet 3 -> 25, Planets 4-8 -> 50 each), covering
-- the topics each planet promises, including the spec's own progression
-- examples ("Good morning. Are you going to work?", "I work at the
-- supermarket", "I worked at the supermarket yesterday", the present/past/
-- future/negative/question drill set, and the surprise-review vocabulary
-- like "quarta-feira"/Wednesday).
--
-- Every sentence is authored once in all three languages and stored in the
-- three "authored" courses:
--
--   (pt,en)  English course  — en = target, pt = base   (the customer's course)
--   (pt,es)  Spanish course  — es = target, pt = base
--   (en,pt)  Portuguese course — pt = target, en = base
--
-- and then mirrored into the three derived courses (es->en, en->es, es->pt)
-- with the same number/position join the full-language-matrix migration
-- (000007) uses, so every one of the six course pairs grows together.
-- Structure fields describe the English sentence (the course that authored
-- the target); the derived courses reuse them exactly as 000007 does.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. English course (pt -> en): target en, base pt
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

